# handshaker ↔ SNANA magcor cross-check

Goal: get the per-band chromatic magcor straight from the SNANA sim and compare
it to handshaker. The sim is run **twice** with identical inputs except the kcor;
the magcor is the difference.

    magcor(band) = mag_reference(band) − mag_ice(band)

where both kcors use the **K-star (KF06T2)** as the mag system, so the result is
the K-giant-referenced magcor (AB primary cancels).

## Step 1 — SIMLIB  (`magcor_test.SIMLIB`) 

One `LIBID`, `NOBS: 7`, exactly one observation per band (R Z Y J H F K) at a
single epoch `MJD = 61010.000`. The same simlib feeds both sims.

Field-by-field (the `S:` line columns):

| col | value | meaning / why |
|-----|-------|---------------|
| MJD | 61010.000 | one epoch for all bands → all share one Trest (step 5) |
| IDEXPT | 1..7 | unique exposure id per obs |
| FLT | R Z Y J H F K | band code; must match the kcor `FILTER:` chars |
| GAIN | 1.0 | placeholder (noiseless truth used) |
| RDNOISE | 5.0 | placeholder |
| SKYSIG | 10.0 | placeholder |
| PSF1/PSF2/ratio | 1.50/0/0 | placeholder PSF (pixels) |
| ZPTAVG | 32.00 | placeholder ZP; only needs to be identical in both runs |
| ZPTERR | 0.005 | placeholder |
| MAG | -99.0 | let the sim compute the mag from the SED+kcor |

Only requirement that matters: **the two runs use the same SIMLIB**, so ZPT/noise
cancel and `magcor` is purely the kcor (filter-system) difference.

`FILTERS: RZYJHFK` / `MWEBV: 0.000` (no Galactic dust).


## Step 2 — template sim-input (TODO)
Template `.input` with `__X1__`, `__C__`, `__Z__`, `__PEAKMJD__`, `__KCOR__`
placeholders for string replacement. Truth-mode flag: if TRUE, fix x1/c/mB to
truth (`GENMEAN`/single-value ranges, `GENSIGMA 0`); if real data, draw from
populations. No dust (`GENRANGE_AV` off / `GENMODEL` with no extinction).

## Step 3 — two kcors (in progress elsewhere)
1. **Reference**: nominal Roman filters + `PRIMARY_SED: KF06T2`, `MAGSYSTEM: KF06T2`.
2. **Ice**: `FILT_ice150` filters + same K-star primary/system.
(See `kgiant_*KF_*.input` on Midway.)

## Step 4 — per-obs inputs
Trest/tobs, redshift, and (truth-mode) x1, c, mB. No Av/Rv.
